<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Mohanpur State</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Mohanpur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A minor chiefship of the Mahi Kantha country in northern Gujarat, one of dozens of small Rajput holdings under British protection.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Mohanpur was one of the many petty estates of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahi-kantha-agency">Mahi Kantha</a> region, held by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> family whose origins are recorded mainly in local tradition. It emerged as a separate holding by around 1600.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Thakor ruled a handful of villages, paying tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaekwads">Gaekwads of Baroda</a> and, after the early 19th century settlements, coming under the supervision of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahi-kantha-agency">Mahi Kantha Agency</a>. Few details of its rulers or internal affairs appear in standard references.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1948 Mohanpur was merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bombay-presidency">Bombay Province</a>, and its villages became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabarkantha-district">Sabarkantha district</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> in 1960.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/mohanpur-state.jpg" alt="Mohanpur State" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Germenfer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Mohanpur_State.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mohanpur</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mohanpur</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1774&amp;focus=mohanpur-state" aria-label="Mohanpur State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6629 1313 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Mohanpur State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6949 1569L7364 1601M6949 1569L7364 1602M6949 1569L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6949 1569h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6949 1569h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1774&amp;focus=mohanpur-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
